      <Comment source="pmngroup">Atbcat-2 (AT1G10070), Atbcat-3 (AT3G49680) and Atbcat-5 (AT5G65780) each encodes a chloroplast branched-chain amino acid aminotransferase. They can complement the yeast leu/iso-leu/val auxotrophy mutant. The location of the enzymes in chloroplast suggested their roles in branched-chain amino acid biosynthesis.</Comment>
